# system dependencies

python3
python3-xlib
x11-apps      # for xwd
imagemagick   # or graphicsmagick-imagemagick-compat, to covert xwd's output to .png

# internal dependencies

make -C ../xtmux              # binary for this testsuite to drive
make -C ../../_font install   # /etc/bfnt/font0..font7

The harnesses run on a 1000x780 screen, not 800x600: xtmux starts at the font size nearest 30
lines on the screen, and 780/26 = 30 is the base size (13x26 cells), which the tests count in.

palette.py   xtmux colours, sampled from a screenshot (no mouse needed): the default
            background and foreground (slots 0 and 7), slot 15, bold, the cube and greyscale.
            Run as: python3 xtmux/tests/palette.py
vt_check.c   the primary screen's text, wrap flags and cursor against a model, for vt.c alone:
             diet gcc -I_lib -I_font -I_sys -o vt_check xtmux/tests/vt_check.c _lib/vt.c && ./vt_check [seeds]
